[2026-09-30T20:50:55.633Z] INFO faser.utils_med: If someone is having an asthma attack without their inhaler, help them sit upright and reassure them. Encourage them to relax and breathe slowly, using muscles in the upper chest and neck to aid breathing. If the attack worsens, becomes severe, or the person becomes unconscious, call emergency services immediately.

Remember not to expose them to cold air as it can exacerbate the attack. If medication like epinephrine is available, it can be administered again if no improvement is seen within five minutes. However, first aid should prioritize keeping the person calm and seeking emergency help.
[2026-09-30T20:50:55.635Z] INFO faser: Generation 2/60 completed in 2.829s
[2026-09-30T20:50:55.649Z] INFO faser.utils_med: If someone is having an asthma attack without their inhaler, help them sit upright and reassure them. Encourage them to relax and breathe slowly, using muscles in the upper chest and neck to aid breathing. If the attack worsens, becomes severe, or the person becomes unconscious, call emergency services immediately.

Remember not to expose them to cold air as it can exacerbate the attack. If medication like epinephrine is available, it can be administered again if no improvement is seen within five minutes. However, first aid should prioritize keeping the person calm and seeking emergency help.
[2026-09-30T20:50:55.651Z] INFO faser.__main__: Answer:
If someone is having an asthma attack without their inhaler, help them sit upright and reassure them. Encourage them to relax and breathe slowly, using muscles in the upper chest and neck to aid breathing. If the attack worsens, becomes severe, or the person becomes unconscious, call emergency services immediately.

Remember not to expose them to cold air as it can exacerbate the attack. If medication like epinephrine is available, it can be administered again if no improvement is seen within five minutes. However, first aid should prioritize keeping the person calm and seeking emergency help.
